# Coverage artifacts. `.coverage` is a SQLite database and appeared untracked and
# UNIGNORED after the first test run that produced one - exactly the shape a broad
# `git add` sweeps in, which is the mechanism behind this repository's own incident.
# The committed-file-type gate does refuse it (verified), but that gate is the
# backstop and this is the primary layer.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
# `inspect.json` is what the Gate's capability-drift step writes from
# `fastmcp inspect` on every run. It sat untracked and UNIGNORED after the
# first run that produced one (found by the 2026-09-08 fastmcp bump), and
# the committed-file-type gate cannot see an untracked file, so this line
# is the only layer.
inspect.json
# `coverage.json` is what `docs/reviews/check-coverage-floors.py` reads, so the
# gate produces one on every run. It was NOT listed here, and `coverage.xml`
# next to it is the reason: an artefact list beside a tool is blind to the
# format nobody added, which is this repository's most-repeated defect.
coverage.json
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/

